    "tips": [
      {
        "id": "days",
        "title": "Days of the week",
        "body": [
          "Monday is **Bbalaza** and Sunday **Ssabbiiti**. Tuesday to Saturday count up from Monday: **Lwakubiri** (day two), **Lwakusatu** (three), **Lwakuna** (four), **Lwakutaano** (five), **Lwamukaaga** (six). Use **ku** for “on”: **ku Lwakutaano**, on Friday."
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "ugandan-time",
        "title": "Ugandan time",
        "body": [
          "The Luganda clock starts at 7 am, around sunrise. **Ssaawa emu** (hour one) is 7 o’clock, **ssaawa bbiri** is 8, and **ssaawa nnya** is 10. Noon and midnight are **ssaawa mukaaga**.",
          "Quick trick: add six to the English time (or subtract six) to get the Luganda hour. Add **ku makya** (morning), **olweggulo** (afternoon) or **ekiro** (night) to be clear."
        ],
        "table": [["Luganda", "Clock"], ["ssaawa emu", "7:00"], ["ssaawa nnya", "10:00"], ["ssaawa mukaaga", "12:00"], ["ssaawa kkumi", "4:00 pm"]]
      }
    ],
    "culture": [
      {
        "title": "Two kinds of jjo",
        "body": [
          "**Jjo** means yesterday, but it can also point to the day after tomorrow or the day before yesterday. Listen for the verb tense, or ask to be sure."
        ]
      }
    ]
